WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.357
On this slide, we are focusing on membership testing.

00:00:03.357 --> 00:00:08.212
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:08.212 --> 00:00:15.797
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:15.797 --> 00:00:17.292
Before clicking Run, predict the output.

00:00:17.292 --> 00:00:23.442
Then run the cell, inspect the result, and change one value or condition at a time.

00:00:23.442 --> 00:00:26.782
Rerun it and explain why the output changed.

00:00:26.782 --> 00:00:31.967
The goal is to understand the relationship between input, process, and output.

00:00:31.967 --> 00:00:34.332
Choose the structure based on meaning.

00:00:34.332 --> 00:00:39.597
Use dictionaries for labeled fields and sets for uniqueness or membership.

00:00:39.597 --> 00:00:44.445
A good data structure makes later code shorter and easier to reason about.
